ity repairs.\\n\\nPrepare the worktree with primary local/bin/worktree-setup.sh. Keep the old hot cache read-only and use normal helper-managed private/new-version dependencies. Never change the global default toolchain or host/account settings. Do not run lake update; materialize the manifest from the authenticated pinned Mathlib dependency graph using the repository's documented upgrade route. No global package installation or other-project changes.\\n\\n### Acceptance\\nFocused compile checks on the pilot before a serialized full build, then full canonical CI including both axiom audits and comparator drift, declaration-link checks where required, independent exact-head review, and normal merge. Public declaration changes must be audited against the old statements; never solve a port error with a stronger hypothesis or weaker bound. Recheck Palomar's live minimum before final artifact validation. This upgrade is a project prerequisite, not permission to submit.\\n\\n## Bound strength\\nEvery bound remains mathematically identical. Any proposed exception is returned to MAIN with evidence, never silently introduced.\",\nresults/telemetry/github-snapshot/open-issues.json:1246:  \"body\": \"<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: palomar-module-packet-p8-20261002 -->\\n### Motivation\\nPalomar preparation #743 and owner B12:A require the complete substantive library to use Lean modules. This is packet P8, following the tested pattern from #744.\\n\\n### Exact scope\\nConvert only the 37 paths listed under P8 in the immutable [ownership inventory](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/blob/05749bb47fb392cd1967f841e0677cb6d674acc7/results/telemetry/palomar-module-packets-20261002.md). The inventory is computed at 97dc6e049b0ce966be18bf8801e14b30c0081919 and assigns all742 original paths exactly once. Use the current merged prerequisites, preserve their changes, and process this packet in increasing recorded import rank. Apply docs/module-conversion.md; no unrelated cleanup or proof changes.\\n\\n### Invariants and acceptance\\nPreserve every theorem statement and error bound. MAIN has authorized the Lean/Mathlib v4.35.0-rc2 upgrade in #756 under owner briefing section9 (Progress Log #27 comment5937082185). Begin on the current main after #756 and this packet's prerequisites merge; preserve that exact toolchain/Mathlib graph throughout the module-only packet. No new sorry or axiom, and no unsafe proof bypass. Run focused Lean checks and a normalized source/statement comparison; maintain necessary generated provenance copies; then canonical CI (including QPBT AxiomAudit and comparator drift), independent exact-head review, and the normal merge gate. Full builds serialize. MAIN owns dispatch and merge; no further workers.\\n\\n## Bound strength\\nEvery existing estimate is unchanged. This packet changes module visibility and imports only.\\n\\n### Nonstandalone and archival inputs\\nRetain the bytes and provenance of the historical telemetry harness as archival text rather than rewriting its original evidence. Rename nonstandalone comparator header/footer templates consistently with their generator/config references. Regenerate real Lean sources with module headers; preserve the four statement meanings and comparator drift checks. Update only the narrow import scanners/tests required for public/meta syntax. Account explicitly for all original paths and every rename; do not hide a substantive source to evade a limit.\\n\\n### Final inventory refresh\\nThe742-file ownership map is the baseline, not a closed inventory. Compact Palomar packets760/762/763 add new source files after that snapshot. Mathlib-only definition modules already use module headers; proof bridges may temporarily use legacy imports until their library dependencies have converted. Before closing this final conversion packet, enumerate every tracked regular Lean file on the actual candidate main (excluding dependency checkout internals) and convert any remaining substantive b